# Optional evaluation extras (blueprint §10.4). NOT needed for `python -m evals.run`:
# the harness (metrics, LLM judge, runner, reports, calibration) uses only the runtime requirements
# (httpx, pydantic, pyyaml). RAGAS is wired in behind an optional adapter, evals/ragas_eval.py, which
# reports itself unavailable when this file is not installed, and runs only with `--ragas`.
#
# Install:   uv pip install --python .venv -r requirements-eval.in
# Pin:       uv pip compile --universal requirements-eval.in -o requirements-eval.txt
#
# Checked 22 Nov against requirements.txt: it resolves with no conflicts (ragas 0.3.1), but adds about
# 79 packages, including datasets, pyarrow, pandas, numpy, langchain-community and tiktoken. That is
# why it stays out of requirements.txt / requirements-dev.txt, CI and the CPU image.
-c requirements.txt

ragas
